// claudinite-tasks-adhoc — the one-off lever beside the recurring ones.
//
// Every other agentic run in this system is a RECURRING task whose precondition
// decides there is work; there was no way to hand the repo's own executor a
// single piece of work, so an ad-hoc ask had to be started by a person in a
// session. This pack is that lever: mark an issue `claude-task`, and the next
// executor run implements it and leaves a pull request.
//
// THE MODEL IS CHOSEN BY LABEL AND CARRIED BY THE TASK. `claude-model:<family>`
// routes a request to one of three sibling tasks, each declaring its own
// `agent_model`. Nothing reads a model out of the work item — that is the
// property that keeps a forged or hand-edited item from buying itself a bigger
// session — so per-issue choice costs one task folder per family and no change to
// the queue's contract at all.
//
// OPT-IN, and no fingerprint: a repo carries this because someone decided an
// agent may implement issues there, which is not a thing to infer from a file
// shape. Declaring it is the decision; removing the declaration is the off switch.
export default {
  id: 'claudinite-tasks-adhoc',
  version: 1,
  minEngineVersion: 4,
  ruleRoutingGuidance: {
    belongs: 'handing this repo one issue to implement — the request labels, who may ask, and the per-model tasks that run it',
    excludes: 'the queue and scheduling contract itself, which is core; recurring task policy belongs to the pack that owns each task',
  },
  badge: 'badge.svg',
  detect: null,
  marker: null,
  seededByDefault: false,
  prose: 'RULES.md',
  worldRules: [],
  // The three tasks live in this pack's own `tasks/<id>/`, discovered structurally
  // by the scheduler's scan rather than declared here.
};
EOF
cat > RULES.md <<'EOF'
# claudinite-tasks-adhoc — handing this repo one issue to implement

An issue in this repo can be marked for the repo's own executor to implement. The mark is a label, the
labels are this pack's alone, and the [README](README.md) carries how the mechanism works.

- **Asking for an issue to be implemented** — apply `claude-task` to it, and optionally
  `claude-model:opus|sonnet|haiku` to choose the model (`opus` when none is given). Nothing else is a
  request: not a sentence in the body, not an assignee, not a comment on its own.

- **Applying `claude-task` on someone else's behalf, or to an issue you did not open** — the run
  checks in code that a person with write access asked: the issue's author, or a commenter who wrote
  `/claude go`. An issue that passes neither is refused once, in a comment, and its label removed.

- **Finding an issue that carries `claude-running`** — a session is implementing it, or one died
  trying. Never clear that label to "retry"; read what the last run said, and re-apply `claude-task`
  only if you mean to start again from where it left off.

- **Writing a `claude-task` issue** — its body is the requirement, and an agent will implement it
  unattended with no one to ask. Say what problem it solves and what "done" looks like; anything you
  would have to answer in a follow-up comment is the part to write down now.
EOF
